WiFi driver library for the Google Pixel 7

The library 'pixel_wifi' is the 'wifi.lib.so' of Genode's WiFi driver
'wifi' (repos/dde_linux/src/driver/wifi) for the phone: a port of the
wireless core of Linux with the vendor's driver for the Broadcom BCM4389
chip and the vendor's driver of PCIe channel 1, the link to the chip. The
driver is configured and used like on other boards, see the README of the
WiFi driver. It needs the ports 'pixel_linux', 'google_soc_gs', and
'bcmdhd_wlan', the driver binary additionally 'wpa_supplicant', 'libnl',
and 'openssl'.

The power management of the link is not used: the chip stays powered and
the link stays out of its low-power states. The phone's boot loader leaves
the PHY of the link isolated, bootstrap releases it.

The firmware of the chip is not part of Genode. The tool
'tool/pull_wifi_firmware' copies it from a phone running Android into the
tar archive 'contrib/pixel_wifi_firmware.tar'. The files are readable for
root only, so the Android build must permit 'adb root' (userdebug, e.g.,
LineageOS).

The scenario 'run/wifi_fetchurl_pixel' connects to an access point and
downloads a page via 'fetchurl'. It takes the access point from the
environment variables GENODE_WIFI_SSID and GENODE_WIFI_PSK, the firmware
from WIFI_FW if given. It needs the repository 'gems' for the pipe file
system of 'fetchurl', and the ports 'curl' and 'lwip':

! adb root
! repos/pixel/tool/pull_wifi_firmware
! make run/wifi_fetchurl_pixel KERNEL=hw BOARD=google_pixel7 \
!      GENODE_WIFI_SSID=<ssid> GENODE_WIFI_PSK=<passphrase>
